        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How do you clean a treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Wipe the handrails, console, belt and deck edges with a dry or barely damp microfibre cloth after each session. Every week or two, unplug it and clean the belt top surface, rails and frame with a cloth dampened in mild soapy water, then a clean damp cloth, then dry. Never spray liquid onto the console, and vacuum around and under the machine.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do you clean a treadmill belt?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Unplug the machine, vacuum loose debris, then wipe the visible belt section with a barely damp cloth and mild dish soap. Advance the belt by hand, keeping fingers away from the rollers, until you have cleaned the whole loop. Go round again with clean water to remove soap, dry it, and let it air-dry fully before use.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can I use disinfectant wipes on my treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Often yes on handrails, grips and the frame, but check your manual, because some manufacturers warn against alcohol, bleach or particular chemicals on the console, screen or belt. Keep the surface wet for the contact time on the label, then wipe with a clean damp cloth and dry. Use the gentlest approved product on screens.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What should you not clean a treadmill with?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Avoid bleach, ammonia, solvents and degreasers, abrasive pads and scouring powders, steam cleaners and hoses, and anything that leaves a film on the belt or foot rails — furniture polish, silicone spray, oily wipes or WD-40. Never spray anything onto the console or toward the motor compartment.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do you clean a treadmill touchscreen?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Turn it off or unplug the machine, then wipe with a soft microfibre cloth that is dry or very lightly dampened with water, or with the screen cleaner your manual names. Never spray onto the screen, and avoid paper towels, ammonia-based glass cleaners and strong chemicals unless the manual specifically allows them.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How often should I clean my treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              A quick wipe after every session, an unplugged clean of the belt, console, rails and frame every week or two, and vacuuming around and under the machine weekly. Clean under the belt and vacuum the motor compartment annually, or every six months on carpet, with pets or with heavy use.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

